# Project Documentation

Document intent at the point of use. Prefer comments that explain *why* or *what the caller gets*, not a restatement of the signature.

Update the comment when behavior changes. Do not leave required declarations undocumented.

## Service functions

Every function in a `services/` module (exported or private) must have a comment immediately above its declaration.

- **Preferred:** a full JSDoc block (`@param`, `@returns`, and `@throws` when relevant).
- **Minimum (simple helpers only):** a one-line `//` comment that states what the function does.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — no comment
export function shouldSubmitLogWatchBatch(values: LogWatchFormValues): boolean {
  return values.episodes.length > 1
}

// ✅ GOOD — simple helper, inline comment is enough
// True when the form should submit as a multi-episode batch.
export function shouldSubmitLogWatchBatch(values: LogWatchFormValues): boolean {
  return values.episodes.length > 1
}

// ✅ BETTER — JSDoc for non-trivial mapping, status, or I/O logic
/**
 * Maps log-watch form values to a single mutation payload.
 *
 * @param options.currentStatus - Existing library status, used to decide status transitions
 * @param options.mediaId - Library media id to attach the watch event to
 * @param options.mediaType - `movie` or `tv`; selects event type and TV context
 * @param options.runtimeMinutes - Optional runtime copied onto the payload when present
 * @param options.values - Submitted form values
 * @returns A `LogWatchInput` ready for the log-watch API
 */
export function toLogWatchInput(options: ToLogWatchInputOptions): LogWatchInput {
  // ...
}
```

## Custom hooks

Every custom hook (`use*` in a `hooks/` module, exported or private) must have a **full JSDoc block** immediately above its declaration. A one-line `//` comment is not enough.

Include `@param` for each argument (and option fields the caller must understand), `@returns` for what the caller gets, and `@throws` when the hook can throw to the caller.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — no comment
export function useTvSeasonEpisodes(
  tmdbId: null | number | undefined,
  seasonNumber: null | number | undefined,
  options?: UseTvSeasonEpisodesOptions,
) {
  // ...
}

// ❌ BAD — one-line comment is not enough for hooks
// Fetches TMDB episodes for a TV season.
export function useTvSeasonEpisodes(
  tmdbId: null | number | undefined,
  seasonNumber: null | number | undefined,
  options?: UseTvSeasonEpisodesOptions,
) {
  // ...
}

// ✅ GOOD — full JSDoc: what the caller gets, when the query runs, and the return shape
/**
 * Loads TMDB episode titles for a TV season when the log-watch UI is open.
 *
 * The query is disabled until both `tmdbId` and `seasonNumber` are present (and
 * `options.enabled` is not `false`). Cached for about an hour.
 *
 * @param tmdbId - TMDB series id; falsy values skip the fetch
 * @param seasonNumber - Season to load; `null`/`undefined` skip the fetch
 * @param options.enabled - When `false`, the query does not run even if ids are set
 * @returns A React Query result for `TmdbTvSeasonDetails`
 */
export function useTvSeasonEpisodes(
  tmdbId: null | number | undefined,
  seasonNumber: null | number | undefined,
  options?: UseTvSeasonEpisodesOptions,
) {
  // ...
}
```
